Message: ['Great question! There *aren’t many songs written *about* specific characters from **Outlander** (like Jamie or Claire) by mainstream artists—but the series *is filled* with powerful, character-driven music that enhances their stories. Here’s a breakdown of standout tracks directly tied to the show and its characters:\n\n---\n\n##  Iconic Theme: *The Skye Boat Song*\n\n- **What it is**: A haunting adaptation of a 19th-century Scottish folk tune (originally about Bonnie Prince Charlie) with lyrics refocused on Claire’s time-traveling journey. It opens every season—performed by Raya Yarbrough, and in season 7 by Sinéad O’Connor \ue200cite\ue202turn0search20\ue202turn0search24\ue202turn0search2\ue202turn0news21\ue201.\n- **Why it matters**: The evolving arrangement reflects the show’s settings—from the Highlands of Scotland to France, Jamaica, and colonial America—while always anchoring back to Jamie and Claire’s Celtic roots \ue200cite\ue202turn0search2\ue202turn0search24\ue201.\n\n---\n\n##  “For My Love That’s Lost” (Outlander: *Blood of My Blood*)\n\n- **What it is**: The brand-new theme for the prequel series, featuring vocals by Julie Fowlis and composed by Bear McCreary. It’s sung in both English and Gaelic and blends evocative lyricism with powerful drum rhythms inspired by a Glasgow street band \ue200cite\ue202turn0news12\ue202turn0news14\ue202turn0search6\ue201.\n- **Why it matters**: Its chorus—“Long the way / O’er the bridge I crossed / For my love… that’s lost”—reflects themes of love, longing, and the interconnected stories of early Fraser and MacKenzie families \ue200cite\ue202turn0news12\ue201.\n\n---\n\n##  Bernard McCreary’s Character-Themed Instrumentals\n\nThough not vocal songs, these instrumental tracks deeply evoke Jamie’s journey and emotions and are beloved by fans:\n\n- **“The Stones Theme” + “Destiny on Culloden Moor” / “A Fraser Officer Survived”**  \n  These underscore emotionally charged moments—especially Jamie\'s farewell at Culloden and the mystical pull of the stones \ue200cite\ue202turn0search7\ue201.\n\n- **“The Fiery Cross” and “Moch Sa Mhadainn”**  \n  Used in Season 5 during the oath-taking ceremony when Jamie lights the fiery cross, with powerful Gaelic vocals capturing the spirit of the Jacobite rebellion \ue200cite\ue202turn0search9\ue201.\n\n---\n\n##  Fan-Made Song Edits on YouTube\n\nThese aren’t official but beautifully capture the *spirit* of Jamie and Claire’s connection:\n\n- **“Tell Me Now” (Jamie ♥ Claire)**  \n  A fan vid using Hans Zimmer’s powerful track “Tell Me Now,” with dialogue and imagery from the show underscoring the couple’s devotion \ue200cite\ue202turn0youtube16\ue201.\n\n- **Jamie’s Song to Claire (by ravelscot)**  \n  Set to the poignant "You" by Keaton Henson, this edit imagines Jamie’s heartfelt vow and connection to Claire \ue200cite\ue202turn0youtube17\ue201.\n\n---\n\n##  Fan Favorites from the Soundtrack\n\nReddit is full of music love for the Outlander soundtrack—here are some favorites:\n\n> “Claire and Jamie’s theme—always gives me goosebumps”  \n> “Dance of the Druids”  \n> “Destiny on Culloden Moor”  \n> “Moch Sa Mhadainn”  \n\ue200cite\ue202turn0reddit28\ue201\n\nThe track “Never My Love” by The Association plays over the Season 5 finale and leaves an unforgettable emotional impact, especially given its placement in a particularly chilling scene \ue200cite\ue202turn0reddit29\ue201.\n\n---\n\n###  Summary Table:\n\n| Song/Theme                                  | Where It Appears                                | Connection to Characters                              |\n|--------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|\n| **The Skye Boat Song**                     | Opening theme of Outlander (seasons 1–7)         | Symbolizes Claire’s journey back in time and anchors Jamie & Claire’s identity |\n| **For My Love That’s Lost**                | Opening theme for *Outlander: Blood of My Blood* | Captures themes of love and family across generations  |\n| **Stones Theme / Dest. on Culloden Moor**  | Season 2 pivotal moments                         | Jamie’s emotional arc and legacy at Culloden           |\n| **The Fiery Cross / Moch Sa Mhadainn**     | Season 5 milestone sequence                      | Jacobite pride and Jamie’s warrior journey             |\n| **Fan YouTube edits (“Tell Me Now”, “You”)** | Fan tributes                                 | Emotional interpretations of Jamie–Claire bond         |\n| **Selected soundtrack tracks (fans)**       | Various scenes                                   | Deep emotional resonance tied to the characters        |\n\n---\n\nIf you\'re looking for a more *official playlist or soundtrack suggestions* that highlight Jamie or Claire, let me know—I’d be happy to point you toward streaming platforms or soundtrack albums featuring these themes!\n\n\ue200navlist\ue202More on the new Outlander prequel theme\ue202turn0news12,turn0news14\ue201']
