eral employee communities**\nIn online forums such as Reddit, there are chatter and rumors about the possibility of a DRP 3.0 for specific agencies:\n\n> “Rumor is that DRP 3 will be offered to specific DoD agencies that didn’t hit their staffing reductions… Won’t be offered DoD-wide.”  \n> “Army is looking DRP with a week-long window in August to apply, with admin leave running through Dec 31.”  \n> “EPA got a limited 3rd DRP right before more RIFs.”\ue200cite\ue202turn0search1\ue201\n\nThese anecdotes suggest there's talk of agency-level DRP 3.0 programs beyond just EPA—but these remain **unverified rumors**, except for EPA’s official rollout.\n\n---\n\n##  Summary: What’s actually confirmed so far\n\n| **Agency**         | **DRP 3.0 Status**                             |\n|--------------------|------------------------------------------------|\n| **EPA**            | **Yes** — DRP 3.0 confirmed and underway\ue200cite\ue202turn0search4\ue201 |\n| **DoD**            | **No confirmed** — DRP 2.0 already completed\ue200cite\ue202turn0search5\ue202turn0search3\ue201 |\n| **HHS**            | **No confirmed** — past DRP offerings, no DRP 3.0 announced\ue200cite\ue202turn0search2\ue201 |\n| **Other agencies** | **Unconfirmed rumors**, especially in DoD/Army channels\ue200cite\ue202turn0search1\ue201 |\n\n---\n\n##  What you can do next\n\n- **Check your agency’s HR or internal announcements** if you work at EPA—there’s a real opportunity with DRP 3.0 there.\n- If you’re at DoD or another agency, consider reaching out to your **HR office or chain of command** to see whether rumors hold substance or if any DRP 3 discussions are in the works.\n- Keep an eye on reputable news sources or internal communications—if new DRP rounds are announced, that’s where they’ll show up.\n\nLet me know which agency you're interested in—EPA, DoD, HHS, or another—and I can help dig into more specific guidance for that organization!"]
